COPY public.frecipe (id, created, modified, editcount, recipename, comment, directions, uppname, imagecount) FROM stdin;
1	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2020-08-20 15:05:00	13	Almond creme with raspberries		Soften gelatin in 1/4 cup cold water. Add 3/4 cup boiling water; stir until dissolved. Stir in cream, honey, and extract. Pour into 6 dessert dishes. Chill for 3 to 4 hours or until firm. Thaw berries, reserving liquid. Add enough water to liquid to measure 1/2 cup. Combine sugar and cornstarch; stir in 1/2 cup liquid and half the berries. Cook and stir until bubbly; cook 2 minutes more. Stir in remaining berries. Cover; chill. Spoon berries over creme to serve. Serves 6.	ALMOND CREME WITH RASPBERRIES	2
3	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Arroz A La Mexicana	(Mexican Rice)	Cut clove of garlic in half.  Cook and stir in oil in 2 quart saucepan over medium heat until brown; remove garlic.  Cook and stir rice in oil until golden, about 5 minutes.  Stir in chicken broth and salsa.  Heat to boiling, stirring occasionally; reduce heat.  Cover and simmer 20 minutes.  (Do not lift cover or stir.)  8 servings. You may also use brown rice for added flavor and texture.  For brown rice, cook in oil about 8 minutes, then simmer about 40 minutes.	ARROZ A LA MEXICANA	\N
5	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Blender Salsa	From LA Times	Place tomatoes in blender container and process 1 to 2 seconds to chop, or chop finely by hand.  Place in small bowl and add green onions, cilantro, yellow and jalapeño chiles and oregano. Mix well.	BLENDER SALSA	\N
7	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Cafe Chocolate	2 servings.	Combine heavy cream with cocoa, sugar and vanilla. Whip together until mixture forms stiff peaks. combine equal parts freshly brewed coffee and hot chocolate. Pour into mugs, top with whipped cream and sprinkles.	CAFE CHOCOLATE	\N
8	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Cafe De Feu	Per serving.	Fill mug 3/4 full with coffee. Add 1 lump sugar and 2 tbspn brandy. Stir until sugar is dissolved. Place second lump in a teaspoon. Soak with 1 tspn warmed brandy. Ignite and allow to burn for a few seconds. Stir into coffee and serve immediately.	CAFE DE FEU	\N
9	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Cafe Vienna	Per serving.	Add 1/8 tspn grond cinnamon to hot coffee. Add sugar and stir with cinnamon stick. Top with whipped cream and remaining cinnamon.	CAFE VIENNA	\N
10	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Caper Butter Sauce		In skillet melt butter; add capers, lemon juice and salt. Serve with fish, chicken or vegetables.	CAPER BUTTER SAUCE	\N
11	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Cathy H. Spareribs/Short Ribs	Cathy Houlberg	Cover ribs with water and add the above ingredients. Bring to a boil then turn heat down to a simmer and simmer for 1 1/2 hours. Coat in barbecue sauce or honey and barbecue.	CATHY H. SPARERIBS/SHORT RIBS	\N
12	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Chicken Breasts Primavera		"1. Cut tops off tomatoes. Gently remove seeds and inside pulp. Put into a strainer set over a saucepan; press with back of a spoon to extract the juice. 2. Cut rest of tomato into 1/4-inch dice and add to a saucepan. 3. Add onion, garlic, 1 1/2 cups olive oil, salt, 1 teaspoon pepper, 2 tablespoons lemon juice and sugar to saucepan. Stir with tomatoes, then let rest in a warm place for 4 to 6 hours, allowing flavors to blend. 4. Tear romaine lettuce into bite-sized pieces, combine with watercress, wrap in a damp towel and place in refrigeration crisper until needed. 5. Stack spinach leaves, 6 at a time, and roll diagonally. Slice on the diagonal into 1/8-inch-wide slivers. Reserve in a damp towel in crisper. 6. Place chicken breasts between sheets of parchment or waxed paper and pound with a wooden mallet or rolling pin until flat. Cut each in half along center seam. 7. Line a 11"x17"x1" cookie sheet with aluminum foil. Place chicken breasts on sheet. Drizzle with remaining olive oil and lemon juice; add rosemary and remaining black pepper. Marinate for 1 hour. 8. To serve, lay out 8 dinner-size plates. Arrange the romaine and watercress in center of each plate. Top each with 1/4 cup tomatoe sauce. 9. Drain marinade. Preheat broiler; place chicken 3 to 4 inches from flame.  Broil 4 to 5 minutes, until chicken is tender. Do not overcook. 10. Place a hot chicken breast on top of each salad. Divide spinach evenly on top of each chicken breast (about 1/4 cup each) and top with remaining tomato sauce. Sprinkle with chopped parsley and serve immediately. Serves 8."	CHICKEN BREASTS PRIMAVERA	\N
13	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Chinese Barbecued Spareribs	Recipe for microwave - Only typed sauce	Ask butcher to cut ribs twice crosswise to make ribs 1 to 2 inches long. At home, cut between each rib to form small pieces. Combine remaining ingredients and coat ribs well with marinade. Cover and marinate at least 1 hour at room temperature, or 2 to 3 hours in refrigerator. Drain and reserve marinade. Wing it from here....	CHINESE BARBECUED SPARERIBS	\N
14	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Chocolate Mousse	Sharon Rubenstein	Melt chocolate in top of double boiler. Beat egg yolks, add sugar gradually, beat. Add yolks and milk to melted chocolate and stir until smooth. Pour into bowl and cool. Beat egg whites until stiff and fold into chocolate mixture. Whip cream and fold into mixture with vanilla and cognac. Pour into 2 quart soufflé dish. Chill thoroughly. Sprinkle top with sifted cocoa. Serves 6 to 8.	CHOCOLATE MOUSSE	\N
15	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Cinnamon Rolls	Ma's recipe.	Defrost all day in refrig. Take out by stove-until defrosted (will raise only a little). Roll and cut. Roll out on flour. Cover in butter, sugar and cinnamon. Let stand about 40 minutes to rise (double in size). Butter pan - 375 degrees for app. 25 minutes until brown.	CINNAMON ROLLS	\N
16	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Cornbread		Mix cornmeal, flour, baking powder, salt and sugar. Set aside. Beat egg. Add milk. Add fat. Add to cornmeal mixture, stir just enough to mix. Fill greased pan half full. Bake at 425 degrees, 20 to 25 minutes, until lightly browned. Yield 6 servings. Cornmeal muffins:  Use recipe for cornbread. Fill greased muffin pans half full of cornmeal mixture. Baking time will be 15 to 20 minutes. Yield 12 servings.	CORNBREAD	\N
17	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Cornish Hen		350 degree oven. 1/4 onion inside each hen.  Season with lemon juice and sage. Put in lemon juice, wine and water. Cook uncovered for 20 minutes each:  Each side, Breast up and baste often.	CORNISH HEN	\N
2	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2022-12-28 10:47:00	1	Apricot Filled Cookies		Cream shortening; add sugar, flavoring and eggs one at a time; beat until light. Add sifted dry ingredients alternately with milk; mix well. Roll to 1/8-inch thickness; cut with scalloped 2-inch cookie cutter. Cut holes in centers of half of cookies with large doughnut cutter. Arrange plain cookies on greased cookie sheets; spread with preserves. Top with remaining cookies; place a small mound of preserves and an almond in center of each cookie. Bake in hot oven, 400 F, about 10 minutes.	APRICOT FILLED COOKIES	0
18	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Creamy Italian Salad Dressing	Variation on Good Seasons Dressing.	Mix the sour cream, mayonnaise and contents of packet. Gradually add milk, stirring until smooth. Makes about 2 cups dressing. Store in refrigerator. For a thinner dressing, more milk can be added a few drops at a time.	CREAMY ITALIAN SALAD DRESSING	\N
19	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Cucumber-Dill Cream	Use on Sesame Crisp Sole, or for other purposes.	Combine all ingredients.	CUCUMBER-DILL CREAM	\N
20	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Curried Lamb		Combine 2 tablespoons flour with salt and pepper. Toss lamb in flour mixture to coat well. Heat oil in a large skillet or dutch oven over medium-high heat. Add lamb; stir and cook until browned. Stir in curry powder and ground ginger; saute until fragrant. Stir in onion, garlic and 1 cup water. Bring to a boil, reduce heat to simmering, cover and cook for 45 minutes or until meat is tender. Stir in cauliflower and apple, return cover and cook 12 minutes or until tender. Mix remaining tablespoon flour with a small amount of water. Add to sauce. Stir and cook until sauce thickens and boils. Serve over rice with a selection of condiments such as raisins, chutney, chopped hard boiled eggs, chopped tomatoes, chopped cucumber, coconut, or chopped peanuts. Makes 4 servings.	CURRIED LAMB	\N
21	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2020-09-21 21:27:00	2	Curry Chicken Delight	Shorten cooking time and update recipe.	"Preheat oven to 350 degrees.\r1. Rinse chicken. Pat dry with paper towels. Coat chicken pieces with flour.\r2. In a skillet, cook bacon until crisp. Drain bacon, crumble & set aside. Reserve drippings. Add chicken to skillet, slowly brown on all sides in hot drippings, about 10 minutes transfer to 8x8"" baking pan.\r3. Bake chicken, uncovered 350 degrees for 30 minutes. Probably should be less ***.\r4. Combine honey, mustard, salt and curry powder. Drizzle over chicken.\r5. Bake uncovered 15 minutes more. Top with crumbled bacon. Serve with hot rice."	CURRY CHICKEN DELIGHT	0
22	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Dilled Croutons		Cube bread into 1/2 inch cubes. Spread cubes evenly over baking sheet. Let dry 2 days or until cubes lose moisture and become hard. Melt butter in large skillet. Pour butter from skillet into a bowl. Add onion salt, parsley and dillweed; mix well. Reheat skillet in which butter was melted. Add croutons; distribute evenly over skillet surface. Pour melted-butter mixture over croutons. Stir to distribute evenly. Fry croutons until golden brown and thoroughly heated; cool. Store up to 1 month in airtight container. Yields 2 quarts.	DILLED CROUTONS	\N
23	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Dried Green Chilies		Cut a lengthwise slit along each of six whole roasted chilies or six canned whole green chilies. Remove the stems, seeds and membranes. Place the chilies on paper towels to drain. Line the bottom of a 12x8 inch flat-bottomed casserole with paper towels. Open the slit chilies and place them in the lined casserole. Microwave at 70% power (med-high) for 7 minutes. Remove chilies from the casserole by lifting the paper towels. Set chilies aside. Place fresh paper towels on the bottom of the casserole. Transfer the chilies back into the lined casserole. Microwave at 70% power for 6 to 7 minutes. Dried chilies should have a paperlike texture. If chilies are not completely dried, repeat procedure. Dried chilies can be frozen for later use.	DRIED GREEN CHILIES	\N
24	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Ejotes Con Hongos	String Beans with Mushrooms	Cook beans according to directions on package; drain well. Saute onions, mushrooms and almonds in hot oil. Add drained beans, pimentos, parsley and butter. Heat for a few minutes. Salt and pepper to taste before serving. Serves 4.	EJOTES CON HONGOS	\N
25	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Enchiladas Camarones	(Shrimp Enchiladas)	Heat oil and cook onion, tomato and green pepper until onions and pepper are tender, about 5 minutes.  Add shrimp and heat for 2 minutes, then remove mixture from heat.  Transfer to large bowl.  Add olives and 1/2 of the grated cheese to the shrimp mixture.  Cover bottom of rectangular glass baking dish with Salsa Verde (see recipe).  Heat tortillas in oil just until soft and limp.  Place some of the shrimp mixture in the center of each tortilla, roll and lay seam-side down in the baking dish.  Coat the surface of each enchilada with Salsa Verde.  Bake 350 for 20 minutes. Serve topped with garnish of shredded lettuce, cheese, green onions, avocado and sour cream. (To substitute scallops instead of the shrimp, cook them slightly longer, but just until tender.  Be sure to drain off any excess liquid before adding cheese and olives.)	ENCHILADAS CAMARONES	\N
26	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	English Muffin Loaves		Combine 3 cups flour, yeast, sugar, salt, and soda. Heat liquids until very warm (120-130 degrees). Add to dry mixture; beat well. Stir in enough more flour to make a stiff batter. Spoon into two 8 1/2 x 4 1/2-inch pans that have been greased and sprinkled with cornmeal. Sprinkle tops with cornmeal. Cover; let rise in warm place for 45 min. Bake at 400 degrees for 25 minutes. Remove from pans immediately and cool.  Makes 2 loaves.  Slice and toast. Makes 16 slices per loaf.	ENGLISH MUFFIN LOAVES	\N
27	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-05-08 14:30:00	0	Ensalada Tricolor	(Mexican Flag Salad)	Heat water and lime juice to boiling.  Place beans in water, bring back to boiling and cook for 5 minutes.  Immediately rinse under running cold water to stop the cooking and drain. Place beans, jicama and red peppers in individual bowls.  Mix Herbed Vinaigrette (see other recipe for this dressing) and chili powder.  Pour 1/4 cup of the vinaigrette mixture over each vegetable.  Cover and refrigerate at least 1 hour. Arrange beans, jicama and red peppers on lettuce leaves in Mexican flag design in a square glass dish, (green on left, red on right).  Place olives in center of rectangle formed by jicama.  6 to 8 servings.	ENSALADA TRICOLOR	\N
