67	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2008-08-20 13:32:00	1	French Bread		In a small bowl, combine 3/4 cup of lukewarm water with yeast and 3/4 cup of flour.  This will make a 'sponge', let it rise about 30 minutes in a warm place.  In a large bowl, combine oil, sugar, salt and cold water.  Add yeast sponge to sugar mixture beating vigorously.  Beat in flour gradually.  Put on a floured surface and knead about 15 minutes.  Place in a bowl.  Cover with a cloth.  Let stand 1 to 1 1/2 hours.  Dough should be double its size.  Press down.  Let stand 15 minutes longer. Separate dough evenly into two pieces. Shape each dough piece into a long tapered loaf.  Place loaves on 2 greased baking pans.  Let stand 1 hour.  Dough should double in size.  Coat tops with egg white.  Cut 1 inch long slits every 2 inches on each loaf top.  Bake at 350° for 45 to 50 minutes until brown.  Egg coating may be repeated during baking.  Use a toothpick to check for doneness.  Remove pans to racks.  Let stand 5 to 10 minutes.  Invert loaves onto a bread board or platter.  Let cool before slicing.  Yields 2 loaves.	FRENCH BREAD	\N
