157	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2021-01-31 21:11:00	2	Basic Pastry - Cuisinart	a basic dough for pies, tarts and quiches	Use metal blade in Cuisinart food processor to process flour, butter (cut into 1 inch pieces first) and salt until mixture is like a coarse meal, about 8 seconds.  Add ice water and pulse until dough begins to clump together.  Do not let it form a ball.  Divide dough and any little scraps into three equal parts and put each in a plastic bag.  Work through bag to press dough together into a ball, then a flat disc.  Refrigerate dough at least 1 hour.  Roll each disc of dough on lightly floured surface to a circle about 1/8 inch thick.  Press into place in pie pan, and follow the pie's recipe to finish.  Makes three pie doughs.  Can be frozen.	BASIC PASTRY - CUISINART	0
