239	2016-02-17 16:01:00	2016-02-17 16:08:00	1	Thai Cucumber Salad	makes 4 servings	Peel the cucumbers, then slice them in half lengthwise. Using a teaspoon, scrape down the center of each half to remove any seeds. Slice the cucumber halves crosswise into thin slices; a mondoline is best, but a knife is fine.  Trim the jalapeno, slice in half lengthwise, then remove the seeds before mincing.\r\rIn a large bowl, add the minced jalapeno, shallots, soy sauce, lime juice and sugar, then stir to combine.  Add the cucumbers and toss to combine. Transfer the mixture to a serving bowl or platter, then top with the cilantro and peanuts.	THAI CUCUMBER SALAD	\N
