241	2016-03-24 17:43:00	2016-03-24 17:54:00	1	Potato-asparagus Soup		Place potatoes in a stockpot and cover with cold water. Cover the pot and bring to a boil, then lower the heat and simmer for 20 minutes or until potatoes are tender.\rMeanwhile, snap the tough ends off the asparagus and discard. Cut the tips of the stalks into 2-inch pieces and the remainder of the stalks into 1/2-inch pieces. Add the asparagus to the potatioes and boil for 3 minutes; drain potatoes and asparagus and set aside.\rRinse out the pot and return to stove over medium heat. Add the oil and heat, then add onion and saute for 5 to 7 minutes. Add the garlic, salt and pepper and saute 2 more minutes. Add the broth and bay leaves, bring to a boil and cook for 10 minutes, then discard the bay leaves. Add the potatoes and asparagus, heat through, then puree three-quarters of the soup in a blender or food processor; return to the pot. Reheat if necessary. Add a squeeze of lemon; serve garnished with fresh dill.	POTATO-ASPARAGUS SOUP	\N
243	2016-08-12 17:32:00	2016-08-12 17:38:00	1	Banana Matcha Green Tea 'Ice Cream'		Peel, slice and freeze the bananas in an airtight container or bag for at least 4 hours or overnight.  Once the bananas are frozen, place them in a food processor.  Process until the bananas have the texture of lumpy oatmeal (about 1 minute). Add the coconut milk, green tea powder and vanilla, then process until very smooth and creamy, about another 2 minutes, scraping down the sides of the processor as needed.\r\rOnce the ice cream is completely smooth, scrape into an airtight container, cover and freeze for 1 to 2 hours for a soft-serve consistency.  For a firmer, more scoop-friendly ice cream, freeze for over 4 hours and allow to temper at room temperature for 10 minutes before scooping.	BANANA MATCHA GREEN TEA ICE CREAM	\N
