255	2017-11-15 13:56:00	2021-02-05 21:51:00	2	Pumpkin Snickerdoodles		1.  Preheat over to 375 degrees. In a medium bowl, whisk together flour, baking soda, cream of tartar, salt and nutmeg.\r\r2.  In a large bowl, whisk together butter, granulated sugar and pumpkin until smooth.  Add egg and vanilla and whisk to combine.  Add flour mixture and stir to combine, about 2 minutes.\r\r3.  In a small bowl, whisk together sanding sugar, cinnamon and allspice.  Drop heaping tablespoons of dough into sugar mixture and roll into 1 1/2-inch balls.  Transfer to parchment-lined rimmed baking sheets, 3 inches apart.  Using a spatula, flatten balls to just under 1/2 inch thick.  Sprinkle with more sugar mixture.\r\r4.  Bake, rotating sheets halfway through, until light golden and firm to touch, 10 to 12 minutes.  Let cool 5 minutes on sheets, then transfer to a wire rack and let cool completely.  Cookies can be stored in an airtight container up to 3 days.\r\rCook's Notes:\rStarting the dough with melted (rather than softened) butter gives this cookie a delightful chew.	PUMPKIN SNICKERDOODLES	0
