289	2020-10-26 16:22:00	2021-03-02 17:36:00	7	Yogurt	Plain yogurt	Take the starter yogurt from the refrigerator so that it has time to get closer to room temperature while you heat the milk.\r\rTo achieve the best results, heat the milk in a double boiler or in a glass bowl on top of a saucepan of boiling water until the milk reaches 185 degrees F (this can also be done in the microwave, whisking the milk after every one minute increment). Do not boil the milk.\r\rLet the milk cool to about 100-110 degrees F before mixing in the yogurt or starter culture packet.  Do not let it cool below 90 degrees F before adding the starter.\r\rUse a whisk to mix the starter yogurt or starter culture with the milk until the consistency is smooth with no lumps remaining.\r\rPut the yogurt mixture in the yogurt maker and cook it for the amount of time shown in the chart.  (9-10 hours when using skim milk.)\r\r**The best way to heat the milk is in a double boiler, but heating your milk in the microwave is a possible shortcut.  Heat the milk in a glass bowl and make sure to stir the milk after each one minute increment.	YOGURT	9
290	2021-01-01 09:58:00	2021-01-01 22:24:00	2	Southern Baked Mac and Cheese	Ryan's recipe	Instructions\r1. Cook macaroni according to the package directions. Drain.\r2. Add butter to skillet, as soon as butter melts whisk in flour. Continue whisking until flour is fully mixed with butter.  Then cook for about a minute to get rid of the flour taste.\r3. Slowly add evaporated milk a little at a time, followed by the half and half; you do not want the mixture to form any lumps. Simmer for about 3-5 minutes until mixture thickens slightly.\r4. Add seasonings, onion and garlic powder, creole seasoning and cayenne pepper.\r5. Bring to a simmer and let it simmer gently for about 2 minutes.\r6. Stir in the cheeses (reserve some as toppings later), and continue stirring until everything's melted and evenly combined and, smooth. Salt & pepper, to taste.\r7. Then add the cooked pasta to the pot, stir to evenly incorporate.\r8. Transfer the pasta mixture into the pan or into a lightly greased 2-qt. baking dish; top with remaining cheese.\r9. Bake at 375 degrees F for 20 minutes or until golden and bubbly.\r\rRecipe Notes\rBread crumb topping (optional)\r- Place a small skillet on medium heat with 2 tablespoons butter, then toss in 1 teaspoon minced garlic, stir for about 30 seconds and throw in bread crumbs. Saute for about 3-4 minutes or until fragrant. Lightly season with salt and pepper, if desired. Then top the mac and cheese with the bread crumbs and bake.\r\rServes 4-5 people\rCalories 492 kcal	SOUTHERN BAKED MAC AND CHEESE	0
291	2021-01-01 10:56:00	2021-01-01 12:15:00	2	Sour Cream Crumb Cake		Makes 12 to 15 servings\r\rThis recipe comes to me from fellow pastry chef Lisa Bell.  She likes to add fresh or frozen berries to the batter, and cinnamon and nuts to the streusel.  I offer this plain version, which lets the flavors of butter and sour cream shine.\r\rPreheat oven to 350 degrees. Butter and flour a 9-by-13-inch baking pan.\r\rIn a small bowl, whisk together the cake flour, baking powder, baking soda and salt; set aside. In the bowl of an electric mixer fitted with the paddle attachment, beat the butter with the sugar at medium speed until light and fluffy, about 2 minutes.\r\rReduce the speed to low. One at a time, beat in the eggs. Scrape the sides of the bowl as needed. Beat in the vanilla. Beat in the flour mixture and sour cream alternately until just combined, ending with the flour.\r\rSpread the batter evenly into the prepared pan.\r\rIn a small bowl, stir together the flour, brown sugar and salt. Using your fingers, work the butter into the flour mixture until mixture begins to clump. Sprinkle the streusel evenly over the batter.\r\rBake the cake in the cener of the oven for 35 to 40 minutes, until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean.	SOUR CREAM CRUMB CAKE	0
292	2021-01-01 12:30:00	2021-01-01 22:25:00	2	Kale, Sausage, and White Bean Soup	Basics Market Recipe	1. Heat olive oil in a sauce pan over medium heat.\r2. Add the onions to the pot and saute until they begin to soften.\r3. Next, add the garlic and sausage.\r4. Continue cooking until the sausage is cooked all the way through.\r5. Add the tomatoes, broth, vinegar and spices and bring everything to a simmer.\r6. Add the beans and continue to simmer for 10-15 minutes, then add the kale.\r7. Simmer for another 5-10 minutes. Serve immediately or store in the refrigerator for up to 7 days.\r8. Alternatively, freeze for up to 2-3 months.\r\rSubstitutions\rYou can use any kind of sausage. If using link sausage, remove from casing.\r\rPortion suggestions, tips and more recipes at basicsmarket.com	KALE, SAUSAGE, AND WHITE BEAN SOUP	0
