309	2022-10-30 13:17:00	2022-10-30 14:37:00	2	Yogurt, Tarragon, Pistachio Pasta Sauce		1.  Fill a large pot with water, place over high heat and bring to a boil. Season lightly with salt, add the pasta and stir, making sure all is submerged.  Cook according to the package instructions, stirring occasionally, until the pasta is al dente, with just a little bit of bite.\r\r2.  While the pasta is boiling, place the yogurt, pistachios, tarragon and oil in a high-speed blender and process until smooth.  Taste, and season with salt and pepper, as needed.\r\r3.  Once the pasta is cooked, drain and add it to a large bowl.  Pour the sauce over it and, using tongs or two big forks, toss to coat.  Sprinkle with tarragon leaves and season with freshly cracked pepper.  Serve, family style, with Parmesan or vegan cheese on the side.	YOGURT, TARRAGON, PISTACHIO PASTA SAUCE	1
159	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2022-11-08 13:03:00	6	Microwave Apple Crisp	from Marge Allen	"In 8" round glass dish arrange apples.  (I use more apples).  In mixing bowl blend remaining ingredients until crumbly.  Spread on apples.  Microwave (High) 5 - 6 minutes, rotating 1/4 turn halfway through cooking.  Apples should be tender.  Can also use red pie cherries, peaches, blueberries, etc. instead of apples.  When using canned fruit, cook 4 - 5 minutes or until fruit is hot.  For rhubarb crisp use 1/2 - 1 cup sugar.  Topping becomes crisper as it cools."	MICROWAVE APPLE CRISP	0
