310	2022-11-15 14:45:00	2022-11-15 14:57:00	4	Kabocha	from Eat Voraciously	1. In a Dutch oven over medium heat, heat the oil until shimmering. Add the onion and bell peppers; cook until they have softened, 5 to 8 minutes.\r\r2. Add the tomato paste, ginger, garlic, cumin, coriander and salt; cook for about 1 minute, until the tomato paste darkens slightly and the spices become fragrant. Add the squash and stir to coat.\r\r3. Pour in the broth and crushed tomatoes; increase the heat to high. Once the mixture begins to boil, reduce the heat to medium or medium-low (enough heat to maintain steady bubbles at the edges); cook, uncovered, until the squash is so tender it breaks apart easily, about 20 minutes.\r\r4. In a medium bowl, thin the peanut butter by combining it with a ladleful of the stew, stirring until smooth and pourable. Scrape the peanut butter mixture into the pot, and stir to combine. Add the cilantro leaves.\r\r5. Use a potato masher to break up the squash (right in the pot), leaving some pieces intact for a chunky texture.\r\r6. Serve with ground jalapeño paste, topped with the chopped peanuts and more cilantro leaves.	KABOCHA	3
281	2019-03-02 11:07:00	2022-12-22 13:48:00	3	Butternut Squash Pie		Place squash in a saucepan with enough water to cover.  Bring to a boil, and simmer over medium heat until tender, about 15 minutes.  Drain, and cool.\r\rPreheat over to 350°.\r\rIn a blender or food processor, combine butternut squash, brown sugar, cornstarch, egg, milk and spices.  Process until smooth.  Pour into the unbaked pie shell.\r\rBake in preheated oven for 50 minutes, or until a table knife comes out clean when inserted in the center.\r\r(optionally you can use a can of sweetened condensed milk and omit the sugar).	BUTTERNUT SQUASH PIE	0
270	2018-02-01 10:42:00	2023-03-17 11:51:00	12	Aebleflaesk	Danish for Apple Pork	Fry bacon until it is slightly soft, not too crispy.  Leave grease in the pan to cook the onions and apples.\r\rPeel and chop a white or sweet yellow onion.  This is optional, but it adds bulk to the dish in a nice way.  Next, chop about one apple per person since they will cook down, into either thin slices or dice.  \r\rLightly saute the onions until golden and translucent in the bacon grease, then add the apples.  At this point, throw in something sweet and savory to the dish; for four apples, add about 2 teaspoons of our desired sweetener and a tablespoon of fresh herbs, such as thyme leaves.  Place a lid over the pan so that everything steams together.  Cook until soft, around 15 minutes.\r \rFinish by mixing in the bacon and adding a dash of salt.	AEBLEFLAESK	6
267	2018-01-20 14:19:00	2023-03-22 10:46:00	5	Jalapeño Sauce		In medium sauce pan combine oil, peppers, garlic, onion and salt.  Saute 4 minutes.\r\rAdd water, cook 20 minutes.  Allow to cool.\r\rTransfer to food processor or blender.  Process slowly adding vinegar.\r\rPut in sterilized jar.	JALAPEÑO SAUCE	0
219	2014-07-28 14:50:00	2023-03-12 13:17:00	2	Pierogi	Eleonore Mickus Recipe	Mix together flour and salt in a large bowl.  Make a well in the flour and add eggs.  Add water and mix with spoon until somewhat blended.  Continue mixing with hands in the bowl until the dough comes together in a mass.\r\rTransfer to a flat surface and continue kneading by hand until the dough is smooth and pliable, about 3-4 minutes.  Divide in half and roll out 1/2 at a time, making sure that it is the 1/8 inch thick or less before cutting and filling.\r\rCut in squares or circles and put filling on the center of each square or circle of dough.  Fold each pierogi in half and crimp edges well.  \r\rWhen you have around 6 to 10 pierogi, drop them in moderately boiling water in a 5 qt pot for about 5 minutes, then remove with slotted spoon.  Rinse with cold water and drain.  \r\rPlace pierogi on waxed paper or cloth towels to dry out for at least 30 minutes before putting them away or frying.  Our family fries them in margarine or butter but some families serve cooked pierogi with sour cream and mushrooms.  Can be frozen.  One recipe makes approx. 50 pierogi.\r\rPotato filling:\r2 potatoes sliced and boiled to tender/soft\r2 tbl butter\rgarlic powder\rcheese shredded\r\r\rCheese filing:  (sweet taste)\r1 Carton DRY cottage cheese (Baker's dry cheese or Farmer's cheese)\r   Note: I you can't find Baker's dry cottage cheese, you may substitiute one carton ricotta cheese.  Empty it into a fine mesh strainer the night before and suspend over a bowl in the refrigerator so the excess liquid can drain.  Continue with the recipe.\r1/2 tsp salt\r1/3 cup sugar\r1 beaten egg\r\rMix all together just before filling the dough as this gets runny when it sits too long.  One carton makes approx. 25 pierogi.\r\rSauerkraut filling:\r1 large can or jar (32 oz.) of sauerkraut\r1 medium onion\rsalt and pepper to taste\rmargarine for frying\r\rRinse, drain and squeeze out excess water from sauerkraut.  Saute onion and add sauerkraut.  Cook until tender, around 1 hour, adding a little water (or Margarine) if it gets too dry.  I make the sauerkraut the night before so that it is dry and cold and is easier to fill the dough.  I can of kraut makes approx. 25 pierogi.	PIEROGI	0
320	2024-09-10 14:43:00	2024-10-13 14:38:00	2	Cole Slaw	classic	1. Mix the dressing in a large bowl, the vegetables will be added later to the bowl. Combine the mayonnaise, vinegars, sugar, celery seed, salt and pepper and mix well.\r\r2. Shred the cabbage by slicing thinly with a knife and add to the bowl. Stir to mix.\r\r3. Shred the carrots using a grater and add to the bowl. Stir to mix.\r\r4. Optionally, add an stir in the raisins.\r\rDon't skip the celery seed, it adds a lot of flavor to this dish. Let the flavors blend in the refrigerator.	COLE SLAW	0
312	2023-04-10 20:38:00	2023-04-10 20:38:00	1	German Potato Salad		In a large pot of salted water over medium-high heat, add the potatoes. Bring to a boil and cook until fork-tender, 15 to 20 minutes. Drain the potatoes in a colander. Slice the potatoes using the thick blade of a food processor and set aside. Slice the onions using the thin blade of a food processor and set aside. Finally chop the parsley using the thin blade.  Place one-third of the potatoes into a large resealable food storage container. Drizzle one-third of the oil over them, then one-third of the vinegar. Top the potatoes with one-third each of the onions, salt, pepper, mustard, paprika, and parsley, in that order. Repeat the process twice. Cool to room temperature, then cover and refrigerate at least overnight.\r\rTurn the container over for several hours so the juices permeate the potatoes. When ready to serve, bring the potato salad to room temperature and serve with a slotted spoon.	GERMAN POTATO SALAD	0
245	2016-12-02 16:46:00	2023-04-15 13:33:00	3	Peppermint Patties		Combine butter, corn syrup, extract and powdered sugar in a mixing bowl. Mix with an electric mixer for about 3 minutes, until ingredients are well combined and are holding together.\rRemove dough from bowl and break off about 2 teaspoon-sized sections. Roll into a ball and gently flatten with your hands. Put patties down on a pan lined with wax or parchment paper. Once all patties are made, place pan in the freezer for 10-15 minutes.\rMelt chocolate in microwave for 1 minute 20 seconds. Let sit for an additional minute in the microwave. Remove and gently stir. Remove peppermint patties from freezer. Use a fork or a handy Wilton Dipping tool like I did to dip each patty in the chocolate, flip to coat the other side, then tap to remove any excess. Transfer chocolate coated patties to wax paper to cool. Top with chocolate jimmies if you’d like.\r\rStore in an airtight container, refrigerate if preferred but it’s not necessary. Yields 40 mints.\r*Add 1 teaspoon peppermint extract, then mix until well combined. Taste dough. If you’d like them to be stronger, add an additional 1/2 to 1 teaspoon extract. You can also use 2 drops of peppermint essential oil instead or even 2 teaspoons mint extract for a more subtle mint flavor. Think Andes Mints as opposed to Starlight mints! Yum.\r**When making candy like this I really find that dipping chocolate just works best. You can purchase Ghirardelli Melting Wafers at most grocery stores. I buy my melting chocolate in bulk on Amazon. If you really want to use chocolate chips instead, I suggest melting 1/2 a tablespoon of shortening or 2 tsp coconut oil in with the chocolate chips, to thin it out and make it easier to dip the candy.	PEPPERMINT PATTIES	0
