48	2008-05-08 14:30:00	2023-12-18 15:24:00	1	Pizza Dough		In a large mixing bowl, make a 'sponge' by mixing the first three ingredients. Let it rise about 30 minutes. Add the remaining ingredients and mix with a wooden spoon. When thoroughly combined, put on a floured surface and knead about 15 minutes (use quick light motions when kneading and a minimum of flour to keep the dough moist. A moist dough makes a light and crisp crust.) Put the dough in a clean bowl that has been rubbed with olive oil and rub the top of the dough with a little more olive oil to prevent a crust from forming. Cover the bowl with a dish towel and put in a warm place, from 90 to 110 degrees. An oven with a pilot light on is a good place. If you have an electric oven, find the warmest part of the house and put the dough there, wrapped loosely with a beach towel. Let the dough rise about 2 hours until it's about double its size. Then punch it down. Let it rise again, about 45 minutes. The dough is now ready for baking or freezing. To freeze, separate it into three equal portions and wrap with plastic wrap. Then put each piece in a plastic bag and freeze. When ready to use, defrost and roll out to fit your baking tin or pizza stone. Bake at 500 degrees for about 15 minutes, depending on the thickness of the pizza. Top with cheese for last few minutes of baking.	PIZZA DOUGH	0
316	2023-11-06 10:38:00	2023-11-06 10:46:00	2	Persimmon Bread		1. Gather ingredients. Preheat oven to 325 degrees F. Oil a 9 x 4 inch loaf pan.\r\r2. In a small bowl, combine flour, cinnamon, nutmeg, cloves, salt, nuts, and raisins.\r\r3. In a large bowl, blend eggs, sugar, and oil. Mix baking soda into pulp, and add to sugar mixture.\r\r4. Fold in flour mixture. Pour batter into prepared pan.\r\r5. Bake for 60 to 70 minutes, or until knife inserted in the center comes out clean.	PERSIMMON BREAD	0
